@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `nii-il33-nouns`
IMPORT `nii-il33-readings`
IMPORT `nii-rounding-regulations`
IMPORT `nii-il33-published-figures`

-- ===========================================================================
-- National Insurance Law s 1 "הסכום הבסיסי", the updating clause for the child allowance. Row IL-33.
-- Source lines 186-189 (paragraph (2), the amounts) and 192, 197 (the updating paragraph (3)).
--
-- WHAT IT SAYS.
--   (2) for the child allowance: (a) for the first and the fifth and later child, 150 new shekels; (b) for
--       the second, third and fourth, 188; (c) for the Income Support Law benefit and the s 68(c) supplement,
--       140 -- each "denominated for 2015" (the notes print 169 / 214 / 158 for 2024-2025 and 173 / 219 / 162
--       for 2026).
--   (3) "from 2015 on, on 1 January of each year, by the rate of rise of the index published last before that
--       day compared with the index published last before 1 January of the previous year; but on 1 January
--       2025 the amounts of paragraph (2) will not be updated and will be in that year as they were on
--       1 January 2024".
--
-- HOW IT IS ENCODED. The amount on 1 January of year Y is the amount of Y-1 raised by the rate of rise of the
-- November index of Y-1 over the November index of Y-2 (nii-il33-published-figures.l4), except that 2025 is 2024.
-- The updated amount is rounded to whole new shekels: regulation 4 of the Rounding Regulations rounds "an
-- amount computed under the Law and used to fix the rate" of the payments of regulations 2 and 3, and the basic
-- amount fixes the rate of the child allowance (the printed notes are whole shekels). The next update starts
-- from the rounded amount: the amount of Y-1 is the figure the Law's notes print.
--
-- FORK U1 (nouns): a fall in the index. The clause speaks of a RISE. Reading 1: no rise, no change.
-- Reading 2: a negative rise lowers the amount. RULED by Meng on 2026-10-08 (SHRUG): declined by default, and
-- declined only where the amounts differ. The tests show that reading 1, with the rounding above, reproduces all
-- six figures the notes print (2024 and 2026), and reading 2 does not (NOTES.md): evidence for reading 1 that
-- is not the text of the Law, and so not the default.
-- Forks U2 and U3 are not switches (NOTES.md, class (b)/(c)): the rise from the index values and from the CBS
-- percentage give the same amounts in every year 2015 to 2026; the rounding is regulation 4's.
-- ===========================================================================

§ `The basic amount of the child allowance, by the updating clause`

§§ `One update`

-- src:197 | (3) לעניין קצבת ילדים המשתלמת לפי הוראות סימן ב׳ בפרק ד׳ – משנת 2015 ואילך – ב־1 בינואר של כל שנה, לפי שיעור עליית המדד שפורסם לאחרונה לפני אותו יום לעומת המדד שפורסם לאחרונה לפני יום 1 בינואר של השנה הקודמת ואולם, ב־1 בינואר של שנת 2025 לא יתעדכנו הסכומים הקבועים בפסקה (2) לרישה של הגדרה זו, והם יהיו באותה שנה כפי שהיו ביום כ׳ בטבת התשפ״ד (1 בינואר 2024);
-- The amount after the update of one 1 January: raised by the rise of the index; a fall handled by the reading;
-- rounded to whole new shekels (regulation 4).
@ref NII s 1 "הסכום הבסיסי" (3), line 197; Rounding Regulations reg 4, line 31; fork U1
GIVEN rd     IS A `The readings this row takes where the text does not decide`
      before IS A NUMBER
      year   IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 1 — the basic amount after the update of 1 January, reading` rd `:` before `updated on 1 January of` year MEANS
    IF   ratio AT LEAST 1
    THEN rounded
    ELSE CONSIDER rd's `a fall in the index, in the updating clause of the basic amount`
         WHEN `a fall in the index leaves the basic amount unchanged` THEN `reg 1 — rounded to whole new shekels:` before
         WHEN `a fall in the index lowers the basic amount by the fall` THEN rounded
         WHEN `a fall in the index is declined where the two readings differ` THEN
             IF   `reg 1 — rounded to whole new shekels:` before EQUALS rounded
             THEN rounded
             ELSE REFUSE "the updating clause raises the basic amount by the rate of RISE of the index; the index published last before 1 January fell against the one before; the text does not say whether the amount is then left as it was or lowered by the fall, and the two give different amounts"
    WHERE
        readings MEANS `the CBS index readings for the update of 1 January of` year
        ratio    MEANS (readings's `the index last published before that 1 January, in the base of the earlier reading`) DIVIDED BY (readings's `the index last published before the previous 1 January`)
        rounded  MEANS `reg 1 — rounded to whole new shekels:` (before TIMES ratio)

§§ `The amount on a 1 January`

-- 2015: the amount "denominated for 2015". 2025: as on 1 January 2024. Before 2015 and after 2026 the clause is
-- outside the deposited data.
@ref NII s 1 "הסכום הבסיסי" (2), (3), lines 187-189, 197
GIVEN nominal IS A NUMBER
      year    IS A NUMBER
      rd      IS A `The readings this row takes where the text does not decide`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 1 — a basic amount denominated for 2015 as` nominal `, on 1 January of` year `, reading` rd MEANS
    IF   year LESS THAN 2015
    THEN REFUSE "the amounts of paragraph (2) of the definition are denominated for 2015 and updated from 2015; a 1 January before 2015 is outside the clause as this row encodes it"
    ELSE IF   year EQUALS 2015
         THEN nominal
         ELSE IF   year EQUALS 2025
              THEN `s 1 — a basic amount denominated for 2015 as` nominal `, on 1 January of` 2024 `, reading` rd
              ELSE `s 1 — the basic amount after the update of 1 January, reading` rd `:` (`s 1 — a basic amount denominated for 2015 as` nominal `, on 1 January of` (year MINUS 1) `, reading` rd) `updated on 1 January of` year

@ref NII s 1 "הסכום הבסיסי" (2)(a)-(c), (3), lines 187-189, 197
GIVEN year IS A NUMBER
      rd   IS A `The readings this row takes where the text does not decide`
GIVETH A `The basic amounts of section 1 paragraph (2), computed by the updating clause`
`s 1 — the basic amounts of the child allowance on 1 January of` year `, reading` rd MEANS
    `The basic amounts of section 1 paragraph (2), computed by the updating clause` WITH
        `under paragraph (2)(a)` IS `s 1 — a basic amount denominated for 2015 as` 150 `, on 1 January of` year `, reading` rd
        `under paragraph (2)(b)` IS `s 1 — a basic amount denominated for 2015 as` 188 `, on 1 January of` year `, reading` rd
        `under paragraph (2)(c)` IS `s 1 — a basic amount denominated for 2015 as` 140 `, on 1 January of` year `, reading` rd

@ref NII s 1 "הסכום הבסיסי"; the ruling of 2026-10-08 (SHRUG)
GIVEN year IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `The basic amounts of section 1 paragraph (2), computed by the updating clause`
`s 1 — the basic amounts of the child allowance on 1 January of` year MEANS
    `s 1 — the basic amounts of the child allowance on 1 January of` year `, reading` `the readings this row takes`
